Feature: Authoring a Compass item and its supporting children

  Recorded live against the GPUI app (sandbox port 8720, SqlOnly / loro=false)
  seeded with a copy of the Compass vault — an index page plus one page per
  Compass kind (mission, problems, goals, strategies, challenges, the
  current/ideal dimension pairs). Every Compass item is an org heading whose
  drawer carries `compass:`, `contributes-to:`, `last-reviewed:`,
  `review-cadence:` and `provenance:`.

  The flow below is the one a Compass user runs constantly: open a Compass
  page, put the caret on the last supporting child of an item, press Enter,
  and type the new supporting line. Live that added a "Measure:" line under a
  goal; here it adds a sibling under the wide seed's page, because the
  vocabulary cannot name a Compass drawer (see NOT RECORDABLE).

  WHY THE `Then` IS THIN. The `Then` half can only match rendered substrings —
  plus the parentage phrasings, which read `SutBackend::block_raw_snapshot()`,
  the same write-side store the composed parentage invariants read. What gives
  these scenarios teeth is the composed catalog running after EVERY step: a
  split that lands the new block under the wrong parent, or that loses the
  original's content, diverges on the next invariant sweep even though no
  `Then` names it. The parentage assertions pin the one thing that mattered
  live: the new supporting line must become a SIBLING of the existing
  children, never a child of one of them.

  NOT RECORDABLE — the whole Compass-specific half of the feature.
  1. TEMPLATE INSTANTIATION. The picker flow (type "/", choose
     `compass-goal`, bind `title`/`metric`/`target`/`mission`/`reviewed`) has
     NO step. `I trigger the slash command on block {block_id}` exists but its
     transition hard-codes selecting "delete", and there is no step that picks
     a named menu entry or supplies template bindings. Driven live through
     `execute_operation instantiate_template` instead — an operation no step
     can express.
  2. DRAWER PROPERTIES. There is no step to set or assert a block property, so
     `contributes-to`, `last-reviewed`, `review-cadence`, `provenance` and
     `compass` are all invisible to a recorded scenario. `I set edge field
     {update} on block {block_id}` covers REQUIRES only.
  3. DISK. The round-trip that matters for Compass — drawer key SET and ORDER
     surviving an edit — needs a disk assertion, and there is none.
  Each of these is reported as a vocabulary gap.

  Scenario: Enter at the end of a supporting line adds a sibling, not a child
    When I focus block "block:structural-page" in region "main"
    And I focus the editor of block "block:c1"
    And I split block "block:c1" at position 2
    And I type "Measure: alpha users use it successfully"
    Then within 10 seconds block "block:c1" is a child of block "block:structural-page"
    And within 10 seconds the widget contains "Measure: alpha users use it successfully"

  Scenario: Indenting a supporting line nests it under the line above
    When I focus block "block:structural-page" in region "main"
    And I focus the editor of block "block:c2"
    And I indent block "block:c2"
    Then within 10 seconds block "block:c2" is a child of block "block:c1"

  Scenario: A Compass item keeps its own text when a sibling is added after it
    When I focus block "block:structural-page" in region "main"
    And I focus the editor of block "block:c1"
    And I split block "block:c1" at position 2
    And I type "Current: unknown"
    Then within 10 seconds block "block:c1" contains "c1"
    And within 10 seconds the widget contains "Current: unknown"
